Acceptance criteria:
The pressed edge visibly lowers and the opposite edge rises for all four
directions. Diagonals lean along both axes at bounded total tilt; opposing
directions cancel that axis while retaining both held marks. Existing
direction marks highlight without new lights, geometry or render passes.
Releasing/cancelling clears marks and returns to the exact rest
pose without delaying native input. Held pointer and keyboard sources share
the native authoritative state. The visible cap surface stays above the deck;
physical hit anchors follow the cross. No GBA, screen, lighting, quality,
native assertion, deadline, retry or deployment-gate changes.

